<title>USA: U.S. 5-year note auction high yield 5.950 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. 5-year note auction high yield 5.950 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Treasury said its Dutch bidding auction of 5-year notes produced these results:</p>
<p>			 5-YEAR NOTES DUE NOV 30, 2001</p>
<p>			     $12.504 BILLION AUCTION</p>
<p>	     YIELD			  PRICE	COUPON</p>
<p> HIGH	5.950    Awarded At	99.680	5.875</p>
<p> MEDIAN    5.910    High Yield	NOT GIVEN  Percent</p>
<p> LOW	 5.850    42 Percent	NOT GIVEN</p>
<p>	   Cover - (Bids Over Amount Sold)    =  2.86 Times</p>
<p> U.S. TREASURY (GOVERNMENT DEBT)		 MATURITY 30.Nov.01</p>
<p> MATURITY/TYPE    5-YEAR NOTES		   PAY DATE 02.Dec.96</p>
<p> TYPE OF DEBT     STRAIGHT			 LAUNCHED 20.Nov.96</p>
<p> ISSUED/ACCEPTED  12.504 BLN USD		 CUSIP   9128272C5</p>
<p> BIDS SUBMITTED   35.821			   COUNTRY	  USA</p>
<p> NONCOMPETITIVE   310.00 MLN			  DUTCH AUCTION</p>
<p> NY FED DISTRICT    N.A.			   COUPON	 5.875</p>
<p> FOREIGN INSTITN   1.320 BLN		     PRICE	 99.680</p>
<p> BIDDING RANGE    5.850-5.950 PCT		YIELD-HIGH   5.950</p>
<p>KEY (HIGH) YIELD DOWN FROM 6.325 PCT AT AUCTION ON 23.OCT.96</p>
<p>KEY (HIGH) YIELD LOWEST SINCE 5.680 PCT AT AUCTION 28.FEB.96</p>
